# env files — NONE are committed.
#
# .env.local and .env.production used to be tracked so `git pull` would carry
# shared config to the server. That was fine while they held only non-secret
# values, but real credentials drifted into them (database password, admin
# password, gateway keys) and were pushed to GitHub. Nothing with a value in it
# is tracked any more.
#
# All configuration now lives in .env.production.local on the server, which is
# never committed and survives `git pull` and `git reset --hard` during deploy.
# .env.example is the only committed env file: keys and documentation, no values.
.env.local
.env.production
.env.production.local
.env.development.local

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
/public/tinymce
